<p>Iran has agreed to a confidential €500 million (about US$589 million) arms contract with Russia to buy man-portable air-defence systems, according to a Financial Times report that Reuters and other outlets relayed. The FT said leaked Russian documents indicate the deal was signed in Moscow in December and covers 500 “Verba” launch units and 2,500 missiles (described as 9M336/associated missiles), to be delivered over three years. If accurate, the purchase would strengthen Iran’s short-range air-defence inventory and underscores deepening practical ties between Tehran and Moscow, including arms-export channels involving Russia’s state exporter Rosoboronexport, as described in the report. The FT said deliveries would come in three tranches between 2027 and 2029.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ryTL6OiHABkeW9C6zIsmxVU5AM8czdLkEQ5tdhktrZqBDIU5IXImtiTBIYrRoCi1I-4OLM3h1EzZIIG5i-GCOxcjAE8iun-ws58LbHkyRxQ4' alt='Russian President Vladimir Putin and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian shake hands as they meet in Moscow, Russia on January 17. — Reuters/File' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Evidence base: The FT said it reviewed leaked Russian documents and spoke with several people familiar with the alleged deal.</li><li>Verification caveat: Reuters said it could not immediately verify the FT report.</li><li>Iran–Russia channel detail: The FT said talks involved Rosoboronexport and the Moscow representative of Iran’s Ministry of Defence and Armed Forces Logistics (MODAFL).</li><li>Wider security context (as reported by Dawn): Dawn noted President Donald Trump said the June U.S. strikes destroyed Iran’s key nuclear facilities, while a preliminary U.S. intelligence assessment at the time said the airstrikes did not destroy Iran’s nuclear capability and only set it back by a few months.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Financial Times: The FT said leaked Russian documents it reviewed—along with accounts from people familiar with the matter—describe a confidential contract for Russia’s Verba MANPADS, meant to help rebuild Iran’s air defences. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/d034cc1a-f5fb-494e-a3c1-466e8e80ed82'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>Reuters: Reuters relayed the main claims but stressed it could not immediately verify the FT’s account. (<a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/iran-agreed-secret-shoulder-fired-missile-deal-with-russia-ft-reports-2026-02-22/'>Reuters</a>)</li><li>Iran and Russia (reported): The FT said the deal was negotiated through Rosoboronexport and the Moscow representative of Iran’s MODAFL, and that Tehran formally requested the systems last July. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975009/iran-agreed-secret-shoulder-fired-missile-deal-with-russia-report-claims'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3344283/iran-agreed-secret-us589-million-deal-russia-shoulder-fired-missiles-reports'>Iran in secret deal with Russia for hundreds of shoulder-fired missiles: report</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/d034cc1a-f5fb-494e-a3c1-466e8e80ed82'>Iran agreed secret shoulder-fired missile deal with Russia</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-agreed-secret-shoulder-fired-missile-deal-with-russia-says-media-report/article70665432.ece'>Iran agreed secret shoulder-fired missile deal with Russia, says media report</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/iran-agrees-e500-million-secret-missile-deal-with-russia-report-ws-e-13982545.html'>Iran agrees €500 million secret missile deal with Russia: Report</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975009/iran-agreed-secret-shoulder-fired-missile-deal-with-russia-report-claims'>Iran agreed secret shoulder-fired missile deal with Russia, report claims</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/iran-agreed-secret-shoulder-fired-missile-deal-with-russia-ft-reports'>Iran agreed secret shoulder-fired missile deal with Russia, FT reports</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/iran-agreed-secret-shoulder-fired-missile-deal-with-russia-ft-reports-2026-02-22/'>The Financial Times reports that Iran had signed a confidential €500 million (US$589 million) arms agreement with Russia in December 2025 to buy 500 9K333 Verba man-portable air-defense systems and 2,500 associated missiles, with deliveries scheduled between 2027 and 2029 under a contract negotiated between Iran&#x27;s defence ministry and the Rosoboronexport.</a> - reuters.com</li></ul>